                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Tetrobot won me over pretty quickly. It's a tiny drill robot that chews up blocks and spits them back out as Tetris pieces, and it was charming from the first level. Working out where to drop an L or a T so I could reach a ledge felt great, and spotting the little Minecraft and Tetris nods in the treasure chests made me smile. My big gripe is that there's no undo or checkpoint. One misplaced block late in a long level sent me back to the start more times than I'd like to admit, and a few of the timed jumps felt heavier than they should. Even so, I beat the main story in about four hours and kept going back for stars. If you like puzzle platformers and have some patience, grab it on sale.",
